    title: "Anchor Text",
    content: "Read the following passages carefully before proceeding:\n\n\"There is also an antitype which now saves us — baptism (not the removal of the filth of the flesh, but the answer of a good conscience toward God), through the resurrection of Jesus Christ.\" — 1 Peter 3:21 (NKJV)\n\n\"…one Lord, one faith, one baptism.\" — Ephesians 4:5 (NKJV)\n\n\"He who believes and is baptized will be saved; but he who does not believe will be condemned.\" — Mark 16:16 (NKJV)\n\nAs you read, consider: How does Peter clarify the relationship between baptism and salvation? What does the phrase 'one baptism' imply for the question of rebaptism? And how does Mark 16:16 balance belief and baptism?",
